                    {
                        "sense_id": "05a2f4eb-c6a4-31aa-9d5f-68a6c6f2885e",
                        "entry_id": "0ac358ea-77aa-3c3e-8a83-da310281bfd4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The fact of being marginalized as deviant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5246ce07-d497-430d-88c2-a8f11dedfe33",
                                "sense_id": "05a2f4eb-c6a4-31aa-9d5f-68a6c6f2885e",
                                "text": "The disclosure of tolerance's hidden phobic lining fits in well with queer theory's embrace of the abject as exhorted by Michael Warner, David Halperin, and Lee Edelman. Embracing difference or culturally ascribed abjection with the aim of overcoming or dissipating it would be both naive and ineffective."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
